ght_2_explanation>\n            }}\n        ]\n    }}\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids); <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n----Reports-----\ncommunity,full_content\r\n1804,\"# Triglycerides and Lipid Metabolism Community\n\nThis community focuses on triglycerides, their role in lipid metabolism, and their implications for health, particularly in relation to cardiovascular diseases and conditions like pancreatitis. Key entities include triglycerides, lipoproteins, and adipose tissue, which are interconnected through various metabolic processes and health conditions.\n\n## Triglycerides as a critical energy source\n\nTriglycerides are essential for energy provision and are a major component of lipid metabolism. They are synthesized primarily in the liver and transported in the bloodstream by lipoproteins. Elevated triglyceride levels are linked to increased risks of cardiovascular diseases, making their monitoring crucial for maintaining health. This is particularly important for individuals with conditions such as hyperlipidemia and pancreatitis, where triglyceride levels can significantly impact health outcomes [Data: Entities (2472, 6107); Relationships (7961, 8860)].\n\n## The role of lipoproteins in triglyceride transport\n\nLipoproteins, particularly very-low-density lipoproteins (VLDL) and chylomicrons, are vital for the transport of triglycerides in the bloodstream. VLDL is produced in the liver and carries triglycerides to various tissues, while chylomicrons transport dietary lipids from the intestines. The relationship between triglycerides and these lipoproteins is crucial for understanding lipid metabolism and the potential health risks associated with dyslipidemias [Data: Entities (6075, 6096); Relationships (9291, 10020)].\n\n## Adipose tissue's role in triglyceride storage\n\nAdipose tissue serves as a key storage site for triglycerides, playing a significant role in energy metabolism. It stores excess energy in the form of triglycerides and releases fatty acids when energy is needed. The function of adipose tissue is influenced by various factors, including the gut microbiota, which can affect overall energy balance and metabolism [Data: Entities (6100); Relationships (14486, 10021)].\n\n## Health implications of elevated triglyceride levels\n\nHigh triglyceride levels are associated with several health conditions, including pancreatitis and cardiovascular diseases. Monitoring triglyceride levels is essential for patients receiving parenteral nutrition and those with metabolic disorders. Elevated triglycerides can lead to serious complications, highlighting the importance of regular health assessments and dietary management [Data: Relationships (7961, 10026)].\n\n## Dietary influences on triglyceride levels\n\nDietary factors, such as the Mediterranean diet and omega-3 fatty acid intake, can significantly influence triglyceride levels. Adhering to a healthy diet is crucial for managing triglyceride levels and reducing the risk of cardiovascular diseases. Alcohol consumption is also linked to increased triglyceride levels, indicating the need for dietary awareness in managing lipid profiles [Data: Relationships (10027, 10023)].\"\r\n\n\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n6121,ESPLENOMEGALIA,\"Esplenomegalia, también conocida como agrandamiento del bazo, es una condición que puede estar asociada con trastornos metabólicos y la acumulación de lípidos en el cuerpo. Esta afección puede desarrollarse en adultos que están recibiendo tratamiento con factores estimulantes de colonias, lo que puede afectar su salud.\",2\r\n2079,HIPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA,\"Hipertrigliceridemia, also known as hypertriglyceridemia, is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of triglycerides in the blood. This condition can arise from various causes, including genetic disorders and acquired conditions. It is particularly concerning for patients with Glycogen Storage Disease I, as well as those receiving parenteral nutrition, where excessive lipid administration can lead to elevated triglyceride levels. \n\nManagement of hipertrigliceridemia often involves dietary adjustments to help control triglyceride levels. In patients on parenteral nutrition, careful monitoring is essential, as excessive lipid intake can exceed the body's ability to clear triglycerides, potentially leading to complications such as pancreatitis and pseudohyponatremia. Overall, hipertrigliceridemia is a significant health concern that requires attention to dietary management and monitoring, especially in vulnerable patient populations.\",24\r\n6069,HIPERLIPIDEMIA FAMILIAR COMBINADA,\"\"\"Hiperlipidemia familiar combinada\"\" es un trastorno genético que afecta entre el 0,5% y el 1% de la población norteamericana. Se caracteriza por una captación reducida de ácidos grasos libres y una sobreproducción de apolipoproteína B y triglicéridos, manifestándose en forma de lipoproteínas de muy baja densidad. Esta condición se hereda de manera autosómica dominante y se asocia con niveles elevados de lípidos en la sangre, incluyendo hipertrigliceridemia y colesterol elevado. Además, puede presentarse como una hiperlipidemia mixta, que puede incluir hipertrigliceridemia aislada o niveles elevados de colesterol. La hiperlipidemia familiar combinada está relacionada con un alto riesgo cardiovascular, lo que la convierte en una preocupación significativa para la salud de quienes la padecen.\",16\r\n6105,VLDL,\"VLDL, or Very Low-Density Lipoprotein, are a type of lipoprotein produced by the liver. They play a crucial role in lipid metabolism by transporting triglycerides and cholesterol from the liver to various tissues in the body. VLDL is particularly associated with conditions such as combined familial hyperlipidemia, which is characterized by elevated levels of lipids in the blood. Overall, VLDL are essential for the distribution of lipids throughout the body, facilitating the delivery of energy and structural components to cells.\",12\r\n6122,DISLIPIDEMIAS,\"Las dislipidemias son trastornos que afectan los niveles de lípidos en la sangre, incluyendo hipertrigliceridemia y otros desequilibrios lipídicos.\",2\r\n6068,HIPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA FAMILIAR,\"Hipertrigliceridemia familiar is a genetic disorder characterized by elevated triglyceride levels in the blood. This condition is transmitted as an autosomal dominant trait, meaning that it can be inherited from just one affected parent.\",3\r\n6160,PANCREATITIS LIPÉMICA,\"Pancreatitis lipémica is a type of pancreatitis characterized by inflammation of the pancreas, which can occur due to the accumulation of chylomicrons and non-esterified fatty acids in the bloodstream. This condition is specifically linked to elevated levels of triglycerides in the blood, which contribute to the inflammatory process.\",2\r\n6162,DEFICIT DE APO C-II,\"El déficit de apo C-II es un trastorno autosómico recesivo que afecta la función de la lipoproteína lipasa, causando acumulación de lipoproteínas en la sangre.\",1\r\n6164,DEFICIT DE APO-V,\"El déficit de apo-V es un trastorno que afecta la unión de lipoproteínas a la lipoproteína lipasa, lo que puede llevar a quilomicronemia.\",1\r\n6163,DEFICIT DE LIPASA HEPÁTICA,\"El déficit de lipasa hepática es un trastorno raro que interfiere con el metabolismo de las lipoproteínas, contribuyendo a la hipertrigliceridemia.\",1\r\n6161,DEFICIT FAMILIAR DE LIPOPROTEÍNA LIPASA,\"El déficit familiar de lipoproteína lipasa es un trastorno genético que causa acumulación de quilomicrones en el plasma, resultando en hipertrigliceridemia.\",1\r\n6166,DÉFICIT DE APO C-II,\"El déficit de apo C-II es un trastorno autosómico recesivo que causa un déficit funcional de la lipoproteína lipasa, lo que lleva a la acumulación de quilomicrones y a niveles elevados de triglicéridos.\",1\r\n6168,DÉFICIT DE APO-V,\"El déficit de apo-V es un trastorno que afecta la unión de las VLDL y los quilomicrones con la lipoproteína lipasa, lo que puede resultar en quilomicronemia.\",1\r\n6167,DÉFICIT DE LIPASA HEPÁTICA,\"El déficit de lipasa hepática es un trastorno autosómico recesivo raro que interfiere con el catabolismo de las VLDL e IDL, contribuyendo a la hipertrigliceridemia.\",1\r\n6165,DÉFICIT FAMILIAR DE LIPOPROTEÍNA LIPASA,\"El déficit familiar de lipoproteína lipasa es un trastorno autosómico recesivo que causa acumulación de quilomicrones en el plasma, resultando en hipertrigliceridemia y manifestaciones como xantomas y hepatomegalia.\",1\r\n6159,LIPIDEMIA RETINALIS,\"La lipidemia retinalis es una condición ocular que se presenta con la hiperquilomicronemia, caracterizada por un aspecto rosado blanquecino de los vasos retinianos.\",1\r\n6171,LOMITAPIDA,Lomitapide is a medication that can be prescribed for severe cases of hypertriglyceridemia.,1\r\n6173,HÁBITOS DE VIDA,\"Lifestyle habits refer to the daily behaviors and practices that can affect health, including diet and exercise.\",1\r\n6174,QUILOMICRONEMIAS,,1\r\n6115,LIPOPROTEÍNA LIPASA,\"Lipoproteína lipasa is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in lipid metabolism, specifically in the breakdown of triglycerides. It facilitates the hydrolysis of triglycerides in lipoproteins such as chylomicrons and very low-density lipoproteins (VLDL). This enzyme is essential for the metabolism of triglycerides and is involved in the processing of lipoproteins in the bloodstream, highlighting its importance in maintaining lipid homeostasis.\",10\r\n6153,\"APO A-I, APO C-III, APO A-IV\",\"Las apolipoproteínas A-I, C-III y A-IV son proteínas que desempeñan un papel crucial en el metabolismo de los lípidos y pueden estar implicadas en la hiperlipidemia familiar combinada.\",1\r\n6155,FENOTIPO IIB DE FRIEDRIKSÖN,\"El fenotipo IIb de Friedriksön se refiere a una forma de hiperlipidemia familiar combinada, que se caracteriza por niveles elevados de colesterol LDL y triglicéridos.\",1\r\n6157,FENOTIPO IV DE FRIEDRIKSÖN,\"El fenotipo IV de Friedriksön se refiere a la hipertrigliceridemia familiar, que es otra forma de trastorno lipídico que puede coexistir con la hiperlipidemia familiar combinada.\",1\r\n6151,RENAL CRÓNICA,La enfermedad renal crónica es una condición médica que implica la pérdida gradual de la función renal y se asocia con un alto riesgo cardiovascular.,1\r\n6152,POLIMORFISMOS DE LIPOPROTEÍNA LIPASA,Los polimorfismos de la lipoproteína lipasa son variaciones genéticas que pueden influir en el metabolismo de los lípidos y están relacionados con la hiperlipidemia familiar combinada.,1\r\n6097,APO B-100,\"Apolipoprotein B-100 (Apo B-100) is a crucial protein involved in the metabolism of low-density lipoprotein (LDL) and is recognized by LDL receptors. It serves as the primary apolipoprotein of LDL, playing a vital role in lipid metabolism and transport.\",4\r\n6108,LIPOPROTEINAS,,4\r\n6128,IDL,IDL (Intermediate-Density Lipoprotein) are lipoproteins that are formed from the metabolism of VLDL and are involved in cholesterol transport.,3\r\n6104,HDLS,High-density lipoproteins (HDLs) are involved in reverse cholesterol transport and are synthesized from the catabolism of VLDL.,2\r\n6102,IDLS,Intermediate-density lipoproteins (IDLs) are formed during the metabolism of VLDL and are involved in lipid transport.,2\r\n6130,LPL,\"Lipoprotein Lipase (LPL) is an enzyme that hydrolyzes triglycerides in lipoproteins, facilitating the release of free fatty acids for tissue use and storage.\",2\r\n6170,FENOFIBRATO,\"Fenofibrate is a medication primarily used to lower triglyceride levels in patients suffering from hypertriglyceridemia. Additionally, it is effective in reducing cholesterol levels and triglycerides in the blood, making it a common prescription for individuals with metabolic disorders.\",3\r\n6098,APO B-48,\"Apolipoprotein B-48 is the main apolipoprotein of VLDL, crucial for the metabolism of lipoproteins.\",2\r\n6119,APO C-II,\"Apolipoprotein C-II (Apo C-II) is a crucial cofactor that plays an essential role in the activation of lipoprotein lipase. This protein associates with lipoproteins and is vital for the metabolism of triglycerides, facilitating the breakdown and utilization of these fats in the body.\",2\r\n6124,APO V,Apolipoproteína V es una proteína que se asocia con lipoproteínas y tiene un papel en la unión de VLDL y quilomicrones con lipoproteína lipasa.,1\r\n6123,QUILOMICRONEMIA,\"La quilomicronemia es una condición caracterizada por niveles elevados de quilomicrones en la sangre, a menudo debido a un déficit de lipoproteína lipasa.\",1\r\n6103,LDLS,\"Low-density lipoproteins (LDLs) are the final product of the VLDL-IDL-LDL metabolic cascade, primarily transporting cholesterol to cells.\",4\r\n6129,LDL,\"LDL (Low-Density Lipoprotein) are the final product of the metabolic cascade VLDL-IDL-LDL, primarily responsible for transporting cholesterol to cells.\",3\r\n6106,APOLIPOPROTEINAS,\"Apolipoproteins are proteins that bind lipids to form lipoproteins, playing critical roles in lipid metabolism.\",2\r\n6131,APO E,\"Apolipoprotein E (Apo E) is a protein involved in the clearance of lipoproteins from the bloodstream, particularly in the metabolism of IDL and chylomicron remnants.\",1\r\n6132,PCSK9,Proprotein Convertase Subtilisin/Kexin Type 9 (PCSK9) is a protein that regulates LDL receptor levels and is involved in cholesterol metabolism.,1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3476,PACIENTE,ESPLENOMEGALIA,Patients undergoing treatment with colony-stimulating factors may develop splenomegaly as a side effect.,548\r\n4632,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,HIPERTRIGLICERIDEMIA,\"